### META
directory_path: testsuite
description: DINS test suite framework per PART 4, PART 5, PART 6, and PART 9
created: 2025-01-28
modified: 2025-11-29
status: active

### FILES
testsuite.py | Main test runner with module discovery
README.md | Test suite documentation and usage

### DIRECTORIES
logs/ | Test execution logs
module_core/ | Core system validation tests
module_installer/ | Installer component tests
module_webui/ | WebUI component tests
module_cli/ | CLI tool tests per PART 5.3
module_web/ | Web endpoint tests per PART 5.2
module_check/ | Check command tests per PART 6.3
module_setup/ | Setup state tests per PART 6.1
module_service/ | Service construction tests per PART 9

### MODULE_STRUCTURE
Each module_* directory contains:
- test_module_*.py: Main test file with run_tests() function
- README.md: Module documentation
- .index: Module metadata

### USAGE
Run all tests: python testsuite.py
Run specific module: python testsuite.py --module <n>
Run multiple: python testsuite.py --module cli web check setup service
Pre-deployment: python testsuite.py --pre-deployment
List modules: python testsuite.py --list

### CLI_INTEGRATION
Tests can also be run via: dinser test [options]
See install/_setup.sh/cli/commands/test.sh

### DEPENDENCIES
Python 3.x required
PyYAML for service tests
No external packages needed for basic tests

### COVERAGE
Per PART 5, PART 6, and PART 9:
- Web endpoint testing (module_web)
- CLI command testing (module_cli)
- Troubleshooting mechanic testing (module_check)
- Setup state management testing (module_setup)
- Service construction testing (module_service)
- Integration with executable scripts

### NOTES
All tests are non-destructive by default.
Online tests (web) are skipped if no server is available.
Setup state tests run in isolated temp directories.
Service tests validate descriptor structure and CLI availability.
